---- ENDF/B-VIII.1    MATERIAL 3013         REVISION 1            3013 1451
----- THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                             3013 1451
------ ENDF-6                                                     3013 1451
                                                                  3013 1451
  Temperatures = 293.6 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 K            3013 1451
                                                                  3013 1451
 HISTORY                                                          3013 1451
 -------                                                          3013 1451
 This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction Physics  3013 1451
 (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University (USA). Eight     3013 1451
 temperatures are available in this library. The inelastic        3013 1451
 scattering cross section libraries for H1 in stoichiometric CaH2 3013 1451
 were developed using ab initio lattice dynamics (AILD) [1,2]. The3013 1451
 Full Law Analysis Scattering System Hub (FLASSH) was used to     3013 1451
 produce MT = 2 (incoherent) and MT = 4 data [3]. This is a novel 3013 1451
 evaluation in the ENDF/B library; by convention, MAT=3013 and    3013 1451
 ZA=3113 are chosen for H1 in CaH2.                               3013 1451
                                                                  3013 1451
 THEORY                                                           3013 1451
 ------                                                           3013 1451
 CaH2 has an orthorhombic crystal structure belonging to the Pnma 3013 1451
 Hermann-Mauguin space group (#62), with three nonequivalent atom 3013 1451
 sites. One nonequivalent site belongs to the metal ion, while the3013 1451
 other two both contain hydrogen atoms. As a result, these        3013 1451
 hydrogen atoms provide distinct contributions to the overall     3013 1451
 frequency spectrum of the material and thus have different       3013 1451
 thermal scattering cross sections. Therefore, a unique evaluation3013 1451
 has been submitted for each nonequivalent hydrogen atom in CaH2. 3013 1451
 The mass and free atom cross sections for H-1 have been used in  3013 1451
 this evaluation, as opposed to the naturally-weighted values. The3013 1451
 total isotopic free atom cross section is taken from MF = 3, MT =3013 1451
 2 of the ENDF/B-VIII.0 nuclide evaluations [4] at 1.0E-05 eV,    3013 1451
 while the incoherent free atom cross section is taken from the   3013 1451
 NIST database [5].                                               3013 1451
